[Routing]
* NEAR TERM (next 1-2 days): extract the GTK/TUI patchbay into a reusable
  native librustyui widget (in librustyaxe), before expanding routing features.
  - Audit existing GTK graph/layout/interaction code and TUI canvas/router;
    reuse proven implementations rather than maintain parallel editors.
  - Common backend-independent graph model: stable block/pin/wire IDs,
    configurable block shapes, typed/directional pins, multiple connections,
    compatibility checks and application callbacks for connect/disconnect.
  - Share selection (including groups), keyboard pin cycling and live wire
    preview, dragging, hit testing, obstacle-aware wire routing, automatic
    layout, pan/zoom, context actions, annotations and undo/redo.
  - Expose serialization hooks for positions, view state and annotations;
    RustyRig owns persistence and existing saved layouts must survive.
  - Keep Cairo/GTK and Unicode/ncurses rendering backend-specific; no GTK
    dependency in the TUI/core. Migrate incrementally without losing GTK
    appearance, shortcuts, mouse/touch interactions or existing features.
  - RustyRig supplies audio/serial/control/PTT graph descriptors and validates
    and executes mutations via its existing core APIs. No DSP, rig, network,
    authentication or PTT authorization logic in RustyUI. Graph snapshots
    remain authoritative; pending previews are not committed connections.
  - Use shared adapter/operations for GTK and TUI, including arbitrary
    supported pin-to-pin patching, wire removal and block properties.
  - Add make test coverage for model, pin compatibility, layout, routing,
    selection, persistence and rejected mutations; exercise both renderers.
  - Later expose the generic widget through RustyScript for custom editors.
  - Resume by defining the common model/API and extracting pure graph logic,
    then migrate TUI and GTK in small testable passes. Design only for now.
* fix disconnecting lines (esp tx.mix -> tx.transport)
* make effects and controls selectable in group (shift/ctrl)
* Resampler block(s) for TX, like RX, so we can downsample if need
* Make streaming TX codecs take 44.1/48khz and downsample as needed
* On adding new modem/effect/control, keep the new item(s) selected, ready to drop by clicking
* Allow chaining effects
* Add visibility toggles for Annotations, Serial, Audio, Controls and PTT,
  hiding each category's blocks and associated wiring
  - replace +Control/Effect/Modem text buttons with 
    an icon (matching the layer toggle) with a red plus overlaid
    in a corner
* Allow connections to multiple input pins from one output
* Make *all* blocks keep position and restore on restart

